<title>USA: Three New England govs seek east-west rail link.</title>
<headline>Three New England govs seek east-west rail link.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Jan 24 (Reuter) The governors of Maine, New Hampshire and Vermont, who met on Thursday at a banking convention at the Sunday River ski area in Maine, proposed a new east-west rail corridor linking their states.</p>
<p>But Maine's Gov Angus King favors a highway. After the meeting, King told reporters it was unusual for the three governors to get together but suggested such sessions should become a regular feature.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
</text>
